# 45. Design rationale

Several design decisions were made intentionally.

## No OpenVPN binary patch

OpenVPN itself was not modified.

Maintaining a custom OpenVPN package would introduce significant upgrade and maintenance overhead.

The helper monitor allows the standard distribution OpenVPN package to remain unchanged.

---

## No journal parsing inside the plugin

The OpenVPN plugin does not invoke:

```text
journalctl
```

and does not parse system logs itself.

This keeps the plugin small and avoids:

- spawning external commands
- systemd dependency inside plugin code
- blocking process execution
- complex log parsing inside OpenVPN callbacks

---

## Runtime files instead of database communication

The helper monitor does not update SQL or RADIUS directly.

It only writes a tiny reason code.

This keeps responsibilities separated:

```text
monitor -> determine reason
plugin  -> RADIUS accounting
```

---

## Default User-Request

If no specific shutdown reason can be detected, the plugin uses:

```text
User-Request
```

rather than inventing a more specific cause.

This avoids reporting false `Lost-Carrier`, `Idle-Timeout`, or `Session-Timeout` values.

---

