Working and tested:

```text
[OK] RADIUS authentication
[OK] Accounting-Start
[OK] Accounting-Stop
[OK] Acct-Session-Time
[OK] Acct-Input-Octets
[OK] Acct-Output-Octets
[OK] Acct-Input-Gigawords
[OK] Acct-Output-Gigawords
[OK] Acct-Terminate-Cause
[OK] User-Request
[OK] Lost-Carrier
[OK] Idle-Timeout
[OK] Session-Timeout
[OK] Framed-Route
[OK] CIDR route parsing
[OK] OpenVPN 2.7 CLIENT_CONNECT
[OK] OpenVPN 2.7 CLIENT_DISCONNECT
[OK] systemd reason monitor
```

Not implemented as part of this work:

```text
[ ] restored background Interim-Update scheduler
[ ] full NAS reboot/admin termination classification
[ ] direct OpenVPN API termination-reason callback
```

The last item depends on information exposed by OpenVPN itself.

---

# 47. Summary

This implementation restores RADIUS accounting functionality to the legacy OpenVPN RADIUS plugin while adapting it for OpenVPN 2.7.

The final session flow is:

```text
RADIUS Access-Request
        |
        v
RADIUS Access-Accept
        |
        v
OpenVPN authentication succeeds
        |
        v
CLIENT_CONNECT
        |
        v
RADIUS Accounting-Start
        |
        v
VPN session
        |
        +-----------------------------+
        |                             |
        | OpenVPN detects termination |
        |                             |
        +-------------+---------------+
                      |
                      v
           termination reason monitor
                      |
                      v
              runtime reason file
                      |
                      v
               CLIENT_DISCONNECT
                      |
                      v
            RADIUS Accounting-Stop
                      |
                      v
              FreeRADIUS / SQL
                      |
                      v
             accounting interface
```

The result is complete per-session accounting with the four termination causes most relevant for VPN operation:

```text
User-Request
Lost-Carrier
Idle-Timeout
Session-Timeout
```

while preserving RADIUS authentication and adding corrected `Framed-Route` handling for client-pushed routes.

